=== file: README.md ===
# Customer complaint triage

This workflow classifies a complaint's urgency, drafts an apology, and routes unresolved or non-urgent complaints to a support reviewer. An urgent draft requires an explicit manager confirmation and a further support-review step. Classifier uncertainty, model failures, and rejected or unclear manager replies fail closed.

## Running it

`Main(complaint_body)` is intended to be invoked by the operator's inbox polling integration with one newly received complaint at a time. The workflow does not fetch inbox contents itself: the SupportInbox endpoint is declared with a read-only, allow-listed GET configuration, but no model agent is given access to it.

Configure the environment values used by the tool declarations:

- `SUPPORT_INBOX_URL` and `SUPPORT_INBOX_TOKEN`
- `SUPPORT_SMTP_HOST`, `SUPPORT_SMTP_USERNAME`, and `SUPPORT_SMTP_PASSWORD`
- `SUPPORT_EMAIL_FROM` and `SUPPORT_EMAIL_TO`

The email tool is deliberately not attached to an agent or invoked by this workflow. The plan specifies only one agent, which reads untrusted complaint text, and provides no separate typed-value-only sender. To avoid giving that complaint-reading agent a send capability, the workflow never sends email; even manager confirmation only advances the draft to human review. Configure a separately governed sender before enabling delivery.

Run `weave check main.loom --no-env` to validate the script and `weave test main.loom` to exercise the scripted workflow cases. Model calls are capped at 12,000 tokens and 20 calls per run.
=== end===

